  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45712\", \"PowerToys#23857\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before: the Quick Access popup always opens in the bottom-right corner, even when the taskbar is on the left or top and the tray is elsewhere. PowerToys#45712 (open, version 0.97.2) asks for the same thing, either autodetecting the tray position or a setting to choose the corner, and you can add your use case there. PowerToys#23857 reported the same behavior back in 0.67.0, but its comment only says it should be fixed in a hotfix and does not describe a fix for this. No workaround or fix is documented in those tickets. For now, the popup will appear in the bottom-right corner when opened from the tray icon.\"}",
